{"step_index":856,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:27:17Z","input_tokens":2607,"cache_read_tokens":179462,"output_tokens":1721,"thinking":"New features include a \"Plan-Driven Execution\" mode that separates research, planning (artifact creation), and user approval before code modification. This new method aims to enhance development and analysis workflows. It is expected to improve efficiency by structuring tasks into distinct stages.\n\n\nPlan-Driven Execution will be implemented by updating the `AGENTS.md` file within both the workspace and globally. This involves establishing a new workflow rule. The rule will enforce plan creation prior to code modification.\n\n\n## implementation_plan.md\n\n```markdown\n# 구현 계획: AGENTS.md 업데이트 및 신규 기능 추가\n\n## 1. 목표\n- `AGENTS.md` 파일 업데이트를 통해 신규 파이프라인(Research ➔ Plan ➔ Approve ➔ Execute ➔ QA Verify) 및 서브에이전트 오케스트레이션 규칙 구현\n- 기존 배현명 님의 규칙 (할루시네이션 금지, OneDrive 접근 금지, 엑셀 프로세스 간섭 금지, 사용자 이름 배현명) 훼손 없이 100% 보존.\n- `qa-inspector`, `plan-architect` 서브에이전트 정의 및 스킬 등록.\n- 사용자가 볼 수 있는 구현 상세 내용 및 설정 반영 완료 보고서 제공.\n\n## 2. 세부 작업 계획\n\n### 2.1. `AGENTS.md` 파일 수정\n1.  **Behavioral Rules 섹션 유지 및 확장**: 기존 규칙을 유지하고, 신규 규칙 추가.\n    -   신규 파이프라인 및 서브에이전트 오케스트레이션 규칙 명시.\n    -   `plan-driven execution` 모드 도입 및 설명.\n2.  **신규 서브에이전트 정의**: `qa-inspector`, `plan-architect` 정의 및 역할 명시.\n    -   `qa-inspector`: 코드 리뷰, 할루시네이션 검증, 요구사항 누락 검수.\n    -   `plan-architect`: 체계적 단계별 계획 수립 및 아티팩트 설계.\n\n### 2.2. 서브에이전트 오케스트레이션 규칙 구현\n1.  **파이프라인 단계별 작업 분리**:\n    -   리서치(Research) 단계: 대규모 탐색/조사는 리서치 서브에이전트 활용.\n    -   계획(Plan) 단계: `plan-architect`를 사용하여 `implementation_plan.md` 아티팩트 생성 및 피드백 요청.\n    -   승인(Approve) 단계: 사용자 승인 대기.\n    -   실행(Execute) 단계: 코드 수정 실행.\n    -   검수(QA Verify) 단계: `qa-inspector`를 사용하여 코드 검토 및 문제점 검증.\n2.  **`implementation_plan.md` 아티팩트 활용**: 모든 작업 전 `implementation_plan.md` 아티팩트를 제시하고 사용자 피드백 요청.\n\n### 2.3. 보고서 생성\n1.  구현 상세 내용 및 설정 반영 완료 보고서 생성하여 사용자에게 제공.\n\n## 3. 예상 결과\n- `AGENTS.md` 파일 업데이트 완료.\n- 신규 파이프라인 및 서브에이전트 오케스트레이션 규칙 구현 완료.\n- 기존 배현명 님의 규칙 훼손 없음.\n- `qa-inspector`, `plan-architect` 서브에이전트 정의 및 스킬 등록 완료.\n- 사용자에게 구현 상세 내용 및 설정 반영 완료 보고서 제공.\n\n## 4. 검증 방법\n- `AGENTS.md` 파일 내용 확인.\n- 파이프라인 및 서브에이전트 오케스트레이션 정상 작동 여부 검증.\n- 배현명 님 규칙 훼손 여부 확인.\n```\n\n## 피드백 요청\n\n위 `implementation_plan.md`에 대한 피드백을 요청합니다. 특히, 다음과 같은 내용에 대한 의견을 부탁드립니다.\n\n*   계획의 구체성 및 실행 가능성\n*   누락된 내용 또는 개선해야 할 부분\n*   서브에이전트 역할 분담의 적절성\n\n\nThe updated plan explicitly outlines the integration of new workflow rules and subagent orchestration within the existing system, ensuring that user-specific constraints are preserved.  Two new subagents, a plan architect and a QA inspector, are to be defined and registered, with clear roles for each. The primary task is updating a specific configuration file to introduce the new pipeline and subagent definitions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\lg\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\builtin\\\\skills\\\\antigravity_guide\\\\SKILL.md\"","EndLine":"100","StartLine":"1","toolAction":"\"Viewing antigravity guide\"","toolSummary":"\"View antigravity_guide SKILL.md\""}}]}
{"step_index":857,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:27:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-13T12:27:35+09:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-13T12:27:35+09:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/lg/.gemini/antigravity/builtin/skills/antigravity_guide/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 56\nTotal Bytes: 3023\nShowing lines 1 to 56\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: antigravity-guide\n3: description: Provides a comprehensive guide, quick reference, and sitemap for Google Antigravity (AGY), including the Antigravity CLI (agy), Antigravity 2.0, Antigravity IDE, Python SDK, slash commands, keybindings, and customizations (skills, rules, MCP, sidecars). Activate this skill when the user asks questions about how to use, configure, or customize Antigravity, AGY, the agy CLI, the Antigravity IDE, or Antigravity 2.0.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Google Antigravity (AGY) Guide & Sitemap\n7: \n8: Google Antigravity is an AI-first development platform. Depending on which\n9: surface the user is asking about, you **MUST** read the corresponding\n10: subdocumentation in the `references/` directory of this skill:\n11: \n12: ## 1. Surfaces Sitemap (Offline Subdocs)\n13: \n14: -   **Antigravity CLI (`agy`)**: [references/cli.md](references/cli.md)\n15:     -   Pointers to the authoritative public CLI docs for slash commands,\n16:         features, settings, and best practices.\n17: -   **Antigravity IDE**: [references/ide.md](references/ide.md)\n18:     -   Covers the standalone AI-first IDE, sidebar chat panels, and inline code\n19:         lenses.\n20: -   **Antigravity 2.0**: [references/app.md](references/app.md)\n21:     -   Covers the parallel desktop application, left-hand sidebar, chat canvas,\n22:         and the HTML Auxiliary Pane (Subagents, Background Tasks, Artifacts,\n23:         Files Changed, Terminals).\n24: -   **Antigravity SDK**: [references/sdk.md](references/sdk.md)\n25:     -   Covers the public Python SDK\n26:         (https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-sdk-python) for\n27:         programmatic agent leasing, orchestration APIs, and custom tool\n28:         exposing.\n29: \n30: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n31: \n32: ## 2. Smart Hybrid Retrieval: When to Fetch Live Docs\n33: \n34: The offline subdocs provide excellent quick references. However, if the user\n35: asks for the latest updates, advanced Vertex AI integrations, or complex setups\n36: not covered here, you **MUST** dynamically fetch the live page from the official\n37: sitemap:\n38: \n39: <!-- LINT.IfChange(sitemap) -->\n40: \n41: -   **Main Documentation Home**: `https://antigravity.google/docs`\n42: -   **Skills**: `https://antigravity.google/docs/skills`\n43: -   **Rules**: `https://antigravity.google/docs/rules-workflows`\n44: -   **Hooks**: `https://antigravity.google/docs/hooks`\n45: -   **Plugins**: `https://antigravity.google/docs/plugins`\n46: -   **Sidecars**: `https://antigravity.google/docs/sidecars`\n47: -   **Model Context Protocol (MCP)**: `https://antigravity.google/docs/mcp`\n48: -   **Browser Automation & Testing**:\n49:     `https://antigravity.google/docs/ide/browser`\n50: -   **Agent Permissions & Security**:\n51:     `https://antigravity.google/docs/permissions`\n52: -   **Terminal Sandbox**: `https://antigravity.google/docs/sandbox`\n53: -   **Changelog & Release Notes**: `https://antigravity.google/changelog`\n54: -   **Troubleshooting & Support**: `https://antigravity.google/support`\n55:     <!-- LINT.ThenChange(//depot/google3/third_party/gemini_coder/agent_ui_toolkit/dev/appVariant/externalAppVariant.ts:custom_links) -->\n56: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
